"""Report the prespecified selected-corner confirmation, with no outcome pooling."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,html,sys
import matplotlib
matplotlib.use('Agg')
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
p=Path(sys.argv[1]);a=json.loads((p/'analysis.json').read_text());v=a['primaryContrasts'][0];old=a['previousScreenSeparate'];esc=lambda x:html.escape(str(x));num=lambda x:f'{x:+.2f}';ci=lambda x:f'{num(x[0])} to {num(x[1])}'
def table(head,rows):return '<table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+esc(x)+'</th>'for x in head)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+esc(x)+'</td>'for x in row)+'</tr>'for row in rows)+'</tbody></table>'
s=['<p class="eyebrow">CENTURY • LABORATORY EVALUATION • NOVEMBER 15, 2026</p><h1>Hot/favorable combined-modifier confirmation</h1>']
s.append('<div class="decision"><strong>'+('The positive effect was replicated.'if a['positiveEffectConfirmed']else'The fixed primary interval did not establish a positive effect.')+'</strong> Fresh paired win-rate change: '+num(v['winChangePoints'])+' percentage points; conservative 95% interval '+ci(v['winInterval'])+'. All 20,480 research outcomes passed full-ledger audit and independent recomputation.</div>')
s.append('<p>This confirms the total selected hot/favorable corner on four fixed copied pairings. The neutral and combined arms use unchanged coefficients and original tactics, healthy squads, balanced simulation sides and fresh study seeds. Earlier screening outcomes are kept separate. Nothing was adopted or deployed.</p><img src="effect-comparison.png" alt="Earlier selected screen and fresh confirmation effect intervals">')
s.append('<h2>Screen and fresh confirmation</h2>'+table(['Study','Matched seeds','Win-rate change','95% interval','Paired score-margin change'],[['Earlier selected screen',old['n'],num(old['winChangePoints'])+' pp',ci(old['winInterval'])+' pp',num(old['scoreMargin']['mean'])],['Fresh fixed confirmation',v['n'],num(v['winChangePoints'])+' pp',ci(v['winInterval'])+' pp',num(v['scoreMargin']['mean'])]]))
s.append('<p>The earlier screen protected a family of four corner comparisons; the fresh confirmation has one prespecified primary contrast. Both sample size and comparison-family protection affect the interval widths. A difference between these point estimates does not by itself establish a true change or coefficient improvement. Fresh winner discordances: '+str(v['changedToFocal'])+' toward the focal club and '+str(v['changedAgainstFocal'])+' against it.</p>')
s.append('<h2>Prespecified reference decisions</h2>'+table(['Pooled reference level','Fresh interval classification'],[['+10 percentage points',a['referenceDecisions']['10']],['+15 percentage points',a['referenceDecisions']['15']]]))
words={'within-reference':'The full interval is at or below the reference.','exceeds-reference':'The full interval is above the reference.','unresolved':'The interval crosses the reference.'}
s.append('<p>Ten-point target: '+words[a['referenceDecisions']['10']]+' Fifteen-point review level: '+words[a['referenceDecisions']['15']]+' These pooled statements apply to the specified four pairings and corner; they are not global ceilings or automatic acceptance rules.</p>')
s.append('<h2>Pairing and side sensitivity</h2>'+table(['Copied pairing','Win change','Four-profile protected 95% interval'],[[b['focal']+' vs '+b['opponent'],num(b['contrasts'][0]['overall']['winChangePoints'])+' pp',ci(b['contrasts'][0]['overall']['winInterval'])+' pp']for b in a['matchups']]))
s.append(table(['Focal simulation side','Win change','Exploratory nominal 95% interval'],[[int(x['swap']),num(x['contrasts'][0]['winChangePoints'])+' pp',ci(x['contrasts'][0]['winInterval'])+' pp']for x in a['primarySides']]))
above=[b['focal']+' ('+num(b['contrasts'][0]['overall']['winChangePoints'])+' pp)'for b in a['matchups']if b['contrasts'][0]['overall']['winChangePoints']>10]
extend=sum(b['contrasts'][0]['overall']['winInterval'][1]>10 for b in a['matchups'])
s.append('<p><strong>Pooled-target qualification:</strong> '+(esc(', '.join(above))+' has a point estimate above +10 points. 'if above else'No pairing point estimate exceeds +10 points. ')+str(extend)+' of four protected pairing intervals extend above +10 points. A pooled interval below ten does not certify a ten-point ceiling for every matchup.</p>')
s.append('<p>Each pairing contributes 2,560 seeds split equally between sides. Profile intervals protect four comparisons; side intervals are nominal exploratory. Complete per-profile, per-side score-margin and cell results remain in analysis.json. No preferred pairing or simulation side was selected.</p>')
s.append('<h2>Physical and disciplinary diagnostics</h2>')
rows=[]
for arm,c in a['cells'].items():
 f,o=c['clubs']['focal'],c['clubs']['opponent'];rows.append([arm,f"{c['focalWinRatePct']:.2f}%",f"{c['meanMinutes']:.2f}",f"{100*f['activeEnergy']:.2f} / {100*o['activeEnergy']:.2f}",f"{100*f['meanFinalEnergy']:.2f} / {100*o['meanFinalEnergy']:.2f}",f"{f['shotsPerMinute']:.3f} / {o['shotsPerMinute']:.3f}"])
s.append(table(['Arm','Focal win rate','Mean minutes','Active energy 0–100, focal / opponent','Final energy 0–100','Shots/minute'],rows))
rows=[]
for arm,t in a['disciplineAndPsychology'].items():
 for role,d in t.items():rows.append([arm,role,d['contacts'],d['fouls'],d['seriousFouls'],f"{d['seriousPctOfFouls']:.2f}%",f"{d['capSaturationPct']:.1f}%"])
s.append(table(['Arm','Club','Contacts','Fouls','Serious fouls','Serious / fouls','Shared psychology cap saturation'],rows))
s.append('<p>Active energy is weighted by active-player time separately for each club. Final energy is a 35-player squad mean. Serious-foul rates use observed fouls as denominator. Fatigue, direct weather kick shifts, contacts/foul rates and all psychology contributions are included in the compact analysis. The direct shared positive odds cap is 0.006; it does not cap the eventual match win-rate effect.</p>')
s.append('<h2>Inputs and scope</h2><p>Hot arm: 35°C, 80% humidity, 35/50 km/h wind/gusts, 5 mm/h rain and 45° direction; quarter-end changes. Heat tolerance focal 1/opponent 0, cold traits 0.5, thermal moderation 0.35. Focal streak +5, opponent −5, focal home. Confidence scale 0.20, home odds 0.004, shared cap 0.006 and frustration scale 1. Neutral dry18 control. The fixed match input date remains November 14 to preserve the same intervention; this confirmation protocol is dated November 15.</p><p>Two arms measure the total selected corner effect. They do not separate weather, tolerance and psychology or produce a new interaction estimate. The study does not cover every league team, all severities/directions, injuries, season histories or halftime adaptation. Halftime adaptation remains unimplemented.</p>')
if a['referenceDecisions']['10']=='exceeds-reference':decision='The fixed candidate exceeds the provisional ten-point target in the pooled tested corner. Review a reduction before any adoption; a changed coefficient requires a separately pinned fresh evaluation.'
elif a['referenceDecisions']['10']=='within-reference':decision='The pooled fresh interval fits the provisional ten-point target in these fixtures. Review pairing sensitivity and the remaining evaluation scope before deciding whether to adopt the candidate.'
else:decision='The fresh sample leaves the ten-point target unresolved. Retain the uncertainty and review the candidate against the agreed modifier budget before defining any additional evaluation.'
s.append('<h2>Evaluation decision</h2><p>'+decision+' No coefficient was tuned, no fixture was replaced, no outcome-driven expansion was performed and no official result was changed.</p>')
s.append('<h2>Verification and reproduction</h2><p>Every full retained research outcome was checked for saved-input identity, SHA-256, gzip/CRC, sporting events projected into scores/statistics, clocks, telemetry and compact-record equality. First-two fixture replay and frozen neutral controls were qualified. A separate direct-sum implementation verified declared contrasts, physical metrics, club denominators and the reference classifications. The frozen v1.0 source lock, original lab fingerprint and separately pinned confirmation harness are retained.</p><p>The compact package contains the plan, exact profiles/manifest, paired outcomes and telemetry, ledger checksum index, audit and recomputation proofs, earlier screening comparison and source patch with reconstruction instructions. Full event ledgers remain separate; compact outcomes alone do not permit a new full-event audit without deterministic resimulation.</p>')
fig,ax=plt.subplots(figsize=(8.2,3.8))
for i,(label,x)in enumerate([('Earlier selected screen\nn=1,024 (four-contrast family)',old),('Fresh confirmation\nn=10,240 (one primary)',v)]):
 mean=x['winChangePoints'];lo,hi=x['winInterval'];ax.errorbar(mean,i,xerr=[[mean-lo],[hi-mean]],fmt='o',capsize=5,color='#24638b');ax.text(hi+.2,i,num(mean),va='center',fontsize=10)
ax.set_yticks([0,1],['Earlier selected screen\nn=1,024','Fresh confirmation\nn=10,240']);ax.axvline(0,color='#75808a',lw=1)
for x in [10,15]:ax.axvline(x,color='#bc742d',ls=':',lw=1);ax.text(x,1.15,f'+{x} pp',ha='center',fontsize=9,color='#8b5422')
ax.set_ylim(-.35,1.45);ax.set_xlabel('Focal win-rate change vs neutral (percentage points)');ax.set_title('Selected hot/favorable combined corner\nConservative 95% paired effect intervals');ax.grid(axis='x',alpha=.2);fig.tight_layout();fig.savefig(p/'effect-comparison.png',dpi=180,bbox_inches='tight');fig.savefig(p/'effect-comparison.svg',bbox_inches='tight');plt.close(fig)
css='body{font:16px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#203041;max-width:1150px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px}h1{font-size:36px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px;margin-top:36px}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#60778a}.decision{background:#eaf3f6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #24638b}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px;margin:18px 0}th,td{text-align:left;padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid #d4e0e5}th{background:#edf3f6}img{max-width:100%;height:auto}@media print{body{margin:12px}table{font-size:10px}h2{break-after:avoid}tr{break-inside:avoid}}'
(p/'Century_Hot_Favored_Confirmation_Report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Century hot/favorable confirmation</title><style>'+css+'</style><body>'+''.join(s)+'</body></html>')
print(json.dumps({'status':'completed','tables':sum(x.count('<table>')for x in s),'primary':v,'references':a['referenceDecisions']}))
